{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad","id":618440,"title":"Children of Gaia Revised: Is it really that bad?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-06T21:31:15-07:00","id":618440,"title":"Children of Gaia Revised: Is it really that bad?","content":"Heard it was the worst thing ever and wanted to learn why that is.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing it involves stereotypical hippies and recreational drug use some how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:09:59-07:00","id":618493,"title":"","content":"I didn't find it to be THAT terrible. Though when I flipped through it I was mostly focusing on the crunch. It seemed to be OK in the history at least. I don't remember much else, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:14:02-07:00","id":618498,"title":"","content":"Yes it is that bad. The whole Garou with Garou sex within a pack, the systems and gifts aren't too bad but the rest of the book as well as some of the rites should be burned in a nuclear reactor, then bombed with a hydrogen bomb, then sent to Malfeas before finally falling to Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:27:39-07:00","id":618511,"title":"","content":"Here's an <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaulta3e2.html\" target=\"_blank\">older thread</a> with a list of some of its most glaring faults.<br /> <br /> Here's<a href=\"http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal-and-friends/kurieg/tribebook-children-of-gaia/\" target=\"_blank\"> the SA skewering</a> of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-07-2015, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:46:56-07:00","id":618552,"title":"","content":"It failed to give the Children of Gaia an actual cultural identity other than their agenda (and a sense of connection with certain human social and political movements of the 20th Century) - which means they'd work better as a multitribal camp than a Tribe as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-07-2015, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T06:51:22-07:00","id":618832,"title":"","content":"It's greatest failure, above all the sex, litany and other messes, was to portray the Child of Gaia as ignorant priviledged people who only -want- to do good, never succeeding.<br /> <br /> If you look at each event the characters in the book are in, there is never any success in their actions. When its just this young pack, it might make sense. But when the Elders of the tribe gather and they -still- all fail to raise a Caern due to BSDs being able to outwit them ( with flaming portapotties, people), it doesn't make you want to play the tribe. Tribebook is supposed to be a celebration of a tribe, not a parody of it.<br /> <br /> More than that, though, notice that none of our leads ever actually suffer from these events. They are witnesses, they might get hurt, but they always have a retreat to go to. It never feels like these guys are actually risking themselves. These guys don't act like warriors or peacekeepers, they act like bunch of young idiots with no goals who just go to the protests/meetings because they want to.<br /> <br /> In short, we see all the flaws of the tribe. But none of the merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T09:53:53-07:00","id":619032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=618832#post618832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, we see all the flaws of the tribe. But none of the merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Also, it comes across as (and I hate to say this in this way, because there are times when it's okay to be &quot;x&quot; because what &quot;x&quot; does is well-written/plotted/conceptualized/what-have-you) very &quot;I'm a fanboi and I got to write this book so I can say this, that and the other plus make shout-outs to my friends...!&quot;. It just... just... it just wasn't simply that it was not well written (plenty of WoD books are guilty of that) -- I could overlook/forgive that, in the broad -- it's just that it was...it was... &gt;breathes for a second and thinks&lt;<br /> <br /> It was *wrong*.<br /> <br /> That's the problem.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to paint a picture of the flaws of the subject matter in question, and it's certainly fine is the picture painted is at once subtle in its indication of said flaws as it may be direct about them, the same as with the subjects merits/strengths.<br /> <br /> But this book doesn't do that, at all.<br /> <br /> It's hamfisted in a manner that disrupts the subject matter unnecessarily for the reader. (Hell, for all the shit that the first Clanbook:Malkavian gets for being laid out the way it was, the meta-narrative and in-narrative aspects *jibe* -- like it or not, the presentation made *sense* relative to the subjects at hand, just as the later Revised version flipped on that and went for better writing over meta-narrative presentation.) With TB:CoG, though, the author-insertion of elements (and some poorly researched ones, at that, in several instances) is just sloppy and doesn't live up to the idea that while very early WoD stuff was a bit all-over-the-place, style and editing-wise, it more-or-less had its shit together by Revised... with this book being one of the glaring missteps along the way.<br /> <br /> What makes it horrible is not simply that it's bad (there are worse), but rather that it's bad *and* mediocre. If it were pure-on Samuel-Haight bad, then we could make fun of it and actually gain something from it in that regard. But I can't even find anything, properly, to &quot;make fun of' about it because it's so both overtly-and-subtly ill-executed it just leaves a bad taste in my mouth (much like, for example, &quot;Gypies&quot; leaves an equally bad taste for many people, though for contextually different reasons).<br /> <br /> &gt;shrugs&lt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T10:52:22-07:00","id":619155,"title":"","content":"Just to build on my previous point - lacking a framework for an actual cultural identity for the CoG, I've just made them a multitribal camp at my table, which I find actually better emphasizes their ideology than them being a distinct tribe does (I can always be convinced otherwise by a truly good in-depth tribal writeup, but unlike the other Tribes they've never gotten one). They're all about unity and equality between the Garou, and potentially the Fera.<br /> <br /> This also makes them look less inept - because in canon the major places in the world where they aren't found in significant numbers are the very places that their dream is realized or being realized: Africa and East Asia. If they're a Camp rather than a Tribe, this makes sense, since Garou who believe in unity equality and peace with the Fera just join the Beast Courts in East Asia, and the Ahadi in Africa. So the Children of Gaia aren't organized there because there isn't a necessity for them to organize toward that end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T12:49:15-07:00","id":619253,"title":"","content":"You know, I've never really understood why everyone hates this book. Yeah, it had some points that I thought were a little goofy, but thematically I thought it totally hit the nail on the head. Being a voice for peace in the <i>Garou Nation </i>-- you know, the people who did the Impergium, the War of Rage and the War of Tears and are just generally homicidal dicks at the best of times -- being a voice for peace in <i>that</i> toxic soup is <i>hard</i>. It's a thankless, endlessly frustrating slog with far more defeats than victories. Moreover their ideology is so far out of whack with the rest of their fellow Garou, that they don't really relate all that well with them (and vice-versa), so you wind up with really unconventional interpretations of Garou culture, the Litany, etc. The Children of Gaia are (at least ideologically) radically different in outlook from the rest of the Garou, and the book highlights that.<br /> <br /> Now, if you don't like the Children of Gaia as a tribe... Well, that's different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 08-07-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T13:11:22-07:00","id":619305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619253#post619253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've never really understood why everyone hates this book. Yeah, it had some points that I thought were a little goofy, but thematically I thought it totally hit the nail on the head. Being a voice for peace in the <i>Garou Nation </i>-- you know, the people who did the Impergium, the War of Rage and the War of Tears and are just generally homicidal dicks at the best of times -- being a voice for peace in <i>that</i> toxic soup is <i>hard</i>. It's a thankless, endlessly frustrating slog with far more defeats than victories. Moreover their ideology is so far out of whack with the rest of their fellow Garou, that they don't really relate all that well with them (and vice-versa), so you wind up with really unconventional interpretations of Garou culture, the Litany, etc. The Children of Gaia are (at least ideologically) radically different in outlook from the rest of the Garou, and the book highlights that.<br /> <br /> Now, if you don't like the Children of Gaia as a tribe... Well, that's different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, none of the other tribes ever factor in the book. We don't see Children of Gaia frustrated trying to broker peace in this book, we don't see them at odds with other tribes.<br /> <br /> We see them fail at the simplest thing. They try to raise a Caern in the middle of woodstock 99, with many of the tribal elders present. And fail spectacularly. We see the viewpoint characters -constantly- break the Veil and spend more time thinking about themselves than their duties. Most of the book focuses on how they fail or are incompetent in various ways.<br /> <br /> If the book was about Coggie's struggle to deal with other tribes and often fail, that would be a different thing and make the book better. But it doesn't, it only focuses on the internal failures of the Coggies, to the point where it is stated in the book itself that the -Shadow Lords- handled uniting tribes in eastern europe better than Coggies because the coggies hid from the violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 08-07-2015, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T13:55:46-07:00","id":619374,"title":"","content":"Well, first, it was a pair of elders who were investigating whether or not it was even <i>possible</i> to open a caern there (this was specifically stated as being in doubt since the dormant caern was very weak and an abandoned air force base was probably not going to be a good location anyway). Also (despite the fact that that <i>wasn't</i> what they were doing), I would challenge the assertion that &quot;raising a caern&quot; equates to &quot;the simplest thing&quot;. Opening a caern is a <i>MAJOR</i> deal, <i>very</i> rare, and sometimes fatal for the participants.<br /> <br /> Second, uniting the tribes and advocating peace is <i>precisely</i> the mutually-exclusive paradox that the Children face. How do you advocate peace to a warrior culture? Answer: You don't -- at least not successfully. The Shadow Lords are better at uniting the tribes because they <i>get</i> the blood-and-guts mentality of the Garou at large.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 08-07-2015, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:14:14-07:00","id":619537,"title":"","content":"I didn't dislike it as much as I did the Revised BF book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:55:41-07:00","id":619560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619537#post619537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't dislike it as much as I did the Revised BF book.</div> </div> </div> </div>While GREECEGREECEGREECEGREECE is pretty irritating, it still has some value in showing how a tribe is usually at odds with the culture which it was associated in earlier editions. Get of Fenris Revised just managed to do a better job in that arena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T18:15:04-07:00","id":619603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619374#post619374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, first, it was a pair of elders who were investigating whether or not it was even <i>possible</i> to open a caern there (this was specifically stated as being in doubt since the dormant caern was very weak and an abandoned air force base was probably not going to be a good location anyway). Also (despite the fact that that <i>wasn't</i> what they were doing), I would challenge the assertion that &quot;raising a caern&quot; equates to &quot;the simplest thing&quot;. Opening a caern is a <i>MAJOR</i> deal, <i>very</i> rare, and sometimes fatal for the participants.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's true that opening a caern is not at all simple, you'd think that raising a caern on such a dangerous location with <i>an entire stadium's worth of human witnesses present </i>would be &quot;the simplest thing&quot; to realize is a BAD idea. The Wyrm is already going to know about the Opening and send as many of its minions as it can to disrupt the opening. And the Coggies knew (or should have known) that the minions were on their way. Opening a caern when there are humans present not only threatens the Veil, <i>it endangers all the humans present</i> because they <i>will </i>inevitably get caught in the crossfire.<br /> <br /> So the Coggies aren't just being inept here, they're being <i>criminally negligent</i>. If the Coggies were this incompetent throughout history, they couldn't claw their way out a paper bag, never mind negotiate the Concord and end the Impergium. That's why the Revised Tribebook portrayal of the Coggies feels so off: it feels so wrong for the Coggies to be portrayed as this incompetent when they <i>did </i>have at least a few very real and large victories against the Wyrm, namely the Concord and the end of the Impergium.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I just realized that U26 said that the Coggies weren't trying to Open a caern at Woodstock '99. Rather than try and re-read TB: CoG again (for fear of having my eyes bleed so profusely that I'd die of blood loss), can someone tell me what all the Coggies were really doing there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619374#post619374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, uniting the tribes and advocating peace is <i>precisely</i> the mutually-exclusive paradox that the Children face. How do you advocate peace to a warrior culture? Answer: You don't -- at least not successfully. The Shadow Lords are better at uniting the tribes because they <i>get</i> the blood-and-guts mentality of the Garou at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more accurate answer to advocating peace to a warrior culture is: Make war on the <i>real </i>enemy: the Wyrm. But create peace between the Tribes and between the Garou and humans. You can't go into a war with a split between you and your allies. That inevitably leads to defeat. And nobody said uniting the Tribes would be an easy task, especially when you have to take the Garou's Rage (simultaneously the Garou's greatest strength and greatest weakness) into account. But the only other alternative is extinction.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Garou's Rage is what prevents them from realizing the Coggies are right. It's just far too easy for the Garou to give in to their Rage. That's what makes the Coggies' mission to unite the Tribes so difficult. But nobody said that anything worthwhile was easy....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-07-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T18:28:26-07:00","id":619615,"title":"","content":"I liked it. At least, I had zero problems with the historical parts of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T18:52:11-07:00","id":619645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619374#post619374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, first, it was a pair of elders who were investigating whether or not it was even <i>possible</i> to open a caern there (this was specifically stated as being in doubt since the dormant caern was very weak and an abandoned air force base was probably not going to be a good location anyway). Also (despite the fact that that <i>wasn't</i> what they were doing), I would challenge the assertion that &quot;raising a caern&quot; equates to &quot;the simplest thing&quot;. Opening a caern is a <i>MAJOR</i> deal, <i>very</i> rare, and sometimes fatal for the participants.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Su-Tehp pointed out above, creating a Caern with so many people is idiotic. Yes, raising a Caern is a big thing, but it has still been done for centuries. So why is the area so poorly cleared, why, when the BSDs attack, do the Elders disappear from the action? Centuries of tradition should still have made sure preparations were made in case there was an attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619374#post619374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, uniting the tribes and advocating peace is <i>precisely</i> the mutually-exclusive paradox that the Children face. How do you advocate peace to a warrior culture? Answer: You don't -- at least not successfully. The Shadow Lords are better at uniting the tribes because they <i>get</i> the blood-and-guts mentality of the Garou at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between promoting peace and being so afraid of violence that they were unable to help the Shadow Lords. Again, tribebook should make you celebrate the tribe, not feel like they failed. Even if Shadow Lords are more brutal, you'd think Coggies would have jumped in on the uniting train pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> But most of the book is not them dealing with other tribes, or asking these questions. It's about this young pack that has no command, no goal and only meander from event to event partying. All other tribebooks have elders tell the stories, and for a reason. If the book had been split with the Elders telling tribe relations/Auspices/breeds/etc. and the youth showcasing different aspects, it would have worked better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T18:57:42-07:00","id":619649,"title":"","content":"I hate the one dimensional portrayal of the tribe. The CoG the authors of the Concord have achieved a broad agreement in the past. Fine the tribe wants to bring the humans more into line with Garou philosophy. Perfect where is the behind the scene political manipulator that uses dirty tricks, and spirits to create a new park. Oh wait that's a Shadow Lord thing. I know where is the outstanding cop that always follows the law and is undercover for Internal Affairs weeding out the corruption in the local police force or the Social Worker helping the abused children? Where is the Ahroun that stands as a wall for his pack while they enact a rite of cleansing to clear the local stream of taint. Where is the Philodox that renders judgment that allows two feuding septs to come to a peace. No the tribebook portrays the CoG as being so involved in human affairs as upper class trust fund kids that it is useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T20:12:43-07:00","id":619707,"title":"","content":"I just re-read the passage and I must admit my memory was a bit off. The bit about the likelihood of the opening was not <i>specifically</i> stated as being in doubt, but upon re-reading it, I feel it was still implied.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619603#post619603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... you'd think that raising a caern on such a dangerous location with <i>an entire stadium's worth of human witnesses present </i>would be &quot;the simplest thing&quot; to realize is a BAD idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyway, again reiterating that that <i>specifically</i> <i>wasn't</i> what the Children were doing there: I would presume that since the moot was being held in the Penumbra, any opening rite would have been held there too. Any combat would likely be confined to the Penumbra. Black Spirals sneaking up on the ritual from the physical side of the Gauntlet would be nearly impossible since a bunch of werewolves in Crinos lumbering about with several thousand witnesses would be challenging (remember that roughly .5% of all humans are <i>totally</i> immune to the Delerium -- so if 10,000 humans are in attendance, the Spirals are pretty much guaranteed an average of about 50 human witnesses that are going to recall the events with<i> total </i>precision when the FBI-SAD investigates). Also, it had been mentioned that the concentration of humans and the emotional state of the gathering meant that the area was being suffused with Gnosis completely independent of anything the Garou might have been doing.<br /> <br /> Given the tribe's ideology vis-a-vis the humans, doing it <i>with</i> all of the people there sort of made sense.<br /> <br /> (also, I mentioned that there were a few bits I found a little goofy with TB:CoG -- The Black Spiral Dancers crashing Woodstock with a bazillion witnesses and nobody takes note of the huge Crinos-fight... Yeah,<i> that </i>was goofy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 08-07-2015, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T23:06:07-07:00","id":619808,"title":"","content":"The bit about all the Garou being in the Penumbra was something I missed. I did mention in the edit of my post that U26 did say that opening the caern was not the main purpose of the Garou gathering at Woodstock, but it was buried in the middle of my post and it was an edit, so my bad if it wasn't prominent enough to be noticed. Sorry about that, U26.<br /> <br /> And yeah, nobody taking note of the huge Crinos fight was just one of the goofy things in that book. Another one of the <i>really </i>goofy things in CoG: Revised was Hack, the lupus of the pack, actually <i>conversing </i>with his homid packmates not only while he's in lupus form, but doing it <i>in the full view of human bystanders</i>. Which means that humans are seeing three or four people talking to a wolf (yes, a <i>wolf</i>, Hack does <i>not </i>look like a dog) <i>and the wolf actually barking back as if in response</i>. &quot;Why no, honored elder, we haven't been breaching the Veil merely by having loud arguments with our lupus member in full view at public places with lots of humans about, why do you ask?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:36px\">*HEADDESK*</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-08-2015, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T23:31:49-07:00","id":619816,"title":"","content":"It would be better if they just went to the Mystery Machine for a trip through the country in search of haunted mansions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T23:37:38-07:00","id":619845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619707#post619707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just re-read the passage and I must admit my memory was a bit off. The bit about the likelihood of the opening was not <i>specifically</i> stated as being in doubt, but upon re-reading it, I feel it was still implied.<br /> <br /> Anyway, again reiterating that that <i>specifically</i> <i>wasn't</i> what the Children were doing there: I would presume that since the moot was being held in the Penumbra, any opening rite would have been held there too. Any combat would likely be confined to the Penumbra. Black Spirals sneaking up on the ritual from the physical side of the Gauntlet would be nearly impossible since a bunch of werewolves in Crinos lumbering about with several thousand witnesses would be challenging (remember that roughly .5% of all humans are <i>totally</i> immune to the Delerium -- so if 10,000 humans are in attendance, the Spirals are pretty much guaranteed an average of about 50 human witnesses that are going to recall the events with<i> total </i>precision when the FBI-SAD investigates). Also, it had been mentioned that the concentration of humans and the emotional state of the gathering meant that the area was being suffused with Gnosis completely independent of anything the Garou might have been doing.<br /> <br /> Given the tribe's ideology vis-a-vis the humans, doing it <i>with</i> all of the people there sort of made sense.<br /> <br /> (also, I mentioned that there were a few bits I found a little goofy with TB:CoG -- The Black Spiral Dancers crashing Woodstock with a bazillion witnesses and nobody takes note of the huge Crinos-fight... Yeah,<i> that </i>was goofy)</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've seen of Caern rites, it is never just in one side. The creatures of the wyrm will come from ALL sides and in numbers.<br /> <br /> But, more importantly, just read how the combat goes. The Elders disappear, and as far as I remember, the kids have to leg it out. And these were THE elders, the cream of the crop, the highest ranking ones in america. Plus, sitting on a opponent to not kill them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619808#post619808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yeah, nobody taking note of the huge Crinos fight was just one of the goofy things in that book. Another one of the <i>really </i>goofy things in CoG: Revised was Hack, the lupus of the pack, actually <i>conversing </i>with his homid packmates not only while he's in lupus form, but doing it <i>in the full view of human bystanders</i>. Which means that humans are seeing three or four people talking to a wolf (yes, a <i>wolf</i>, Hack does <i>not </i>look like a dog) <i>and the wolf actually barking back as if in response</i>. &quot;Why no, honored elder, we haven't been breaching the Veil merely by having loud arguments with our lupus member in full view at public places with lots of humans about, why do you ask?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:36px\">*HEADDESK*</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hack is bad, but so is Joe(sp?), who is the pack ragabash, Hacker, knowledge database, Spirit speaker,etc. Or Rich, the so-called theurge of the pack who is basically there to angst about his dad and lounge in hispo in public and do no theurge things at all. Or Ringer, who is more defined by his sexuality than anything.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T01:00:48-07:00","id":619867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619603#post619603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so my bad if it wasn't prominent enough to be noticed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no, I wasn't harping on you. It just seemed that certain <i>other</i> people <i>still</i> didn't seem to get that bit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619603#post619603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rather than try and re-read TB: CoG again (for fear of having my eyes bleed so profusely that I'd die of blood loss), can someone tell me what all the Coggies were really doing there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Moot.<br /> <br /> Holding a moot, I mean.<br /> <br /> Because it's <i>Woodstock</i>.<br /> <br /> Because where <i>else</i> would the Children hold a <i>Child of Gaia Concolation</i>? (Maybe it's just my cheesy sense of humor, but I sort of liked that little touch)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T05:16:10-07:00","id":619929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619253#post619253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've never really understood why everyone hates this book. Yeah, it had some points that I thought were a little goofy, but thematically I thought it totally hit the nail on the head. Being a voice for peace in the <i>Garou Nation </i>-- you know, the people who did the Impergium, the War of Rage and the War of Tears and are just generally homicidal dicks at the best of times -- being a voice for peace in <i>that</i> toxic soup is <i>hard</i>. It's a thankless, endlessly frustrating slog with far more defeats than victories. Moreover their ideology is so far out of whack with the rest of their fellow Garou, that they don't really relate all that well with them (and vice-versa), so you wind up with really unconventional interpretations of Garou culture, the Litany, etc. The Children of Gaia are (at least ideologically) radically different in outlook from the rest of the Garou, and the book highlights that.<br /> <br /> Now, if you don't like the Children of Gaia as a tribe... Well, that's different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the &quot;last words&quot; in the book when it talks what peace actually is are spot on, unfortunately it doesnt carry that in the rest of the book.<br /> <br /> The garous we are presented as POV arent the voice of peace, they are entitle idiots. They views on other tribal views are the point where i wish a proper CoG slap this clowns on the head and told them to get a job and the narrative was just a set up to a joke and we move on to a better pov. <br /> <br /> An example to me is when the BSD attack a fomori tries to get a cog kin and one of the scoobys grapples the fomori. The kin, the only character written acordinly pulls a switch blade but noo, the scooby says that there has being enough blood shed today.......no, just no. Fomoris cannot be saved, once a fomori is made the only thing to do is kill it so the &quot;peaceful&quot; route is just let that poor abomination keep on living or risk it getting waking up and killing more people.<br /> <br /> While they have the peace idiology, they also are garous who fight the wyrm, no hippie-trustfundkid talk about peace change that fact and the books doesnt adress it. W20 in two lines defined the CoGs better than the tribebook.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Children of Gaia\u2019s primary purpose is that of all Garou fight the Wyrm, wherever it breeds and wherever it dwells. But their chosen secondary purpose is to mediate disputes and alliances among septs and packs, strengthening the Nation as a whole.&quot;<br /> <br /> They arent necesarily the good and kind garous like that scooby gang in the tribebook, they are the tribe that get everyone working together. Some might go with the whole love and compasion while others can go with the &quot;peace by any means nescesary&quot;<br /> <br /> If they ever make another tribebook and for some reason they decide to go with the POV approach, i wish it is made after the event of the tribebook in which an elder grabs that bunch of clowns and descontruct every single moronic thing they said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T05:42:37-07:00","id":619945,"title":"","content":"Or maybe it is done with just one of them, the sole survivor of their idiocy, now older, wiser, and miserable for what he was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T06:55:21-07:00","id":619971,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread makes me appreciate the old tribebook more; especially the opening fiction. You had a Garou that despite being betrayed, stabbed with a silver knife and left to die in a Wyrm infested area, still made it through. He used compassion towards a tortured pattern spider to get it to help him kick Wyrm ass. So when he comes back with a big trophy of his victory, his naysayers immediately agree to his pact. That's how I've seen the CoGs: heartfelt, see the big picture, but are tough as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T08:43:47-07:00","id":620062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619929#post619929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the &quot;last words&quot; in the book when it talks what peace actually is are spot on, unfortunately it doesnt carry that in the rest of the book.<br /> <br /> The garous we are presented as POV arent the voice of peace, they are entitle idiots. They views on other tribal views are the point where i wish a proper CoG slap this clowns on the head and told them to get a job and the narrative was just a set up to a joke and we move on to a better pov.<br /> <br /> An example to me is when the BSD attack a fomori tries to get a cog kin and one of the scoobys grapples the fomori. The kin, the only character written acordinly pulls a switch blade but noo, the scooby says that there has being enough blood shed today.......no, just no. Fomoris cannot be saved, once a fomori is made the only thing to do is kill it so the &quot;peaceful&quot; route is just let that poor abomination keep on living or risk it getting waking up and killing more people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically you can save fomori, but it relies on the fomor not being too far gone, and also requires a lot of additional effort that most Garou won't make for practical reasons (Exorcism and someone standing by with Mother's Touch or the like) and might still not work. Even the Gurahl rite made for this purpose isn't a sure bet. So it'd be more accurate to say that it's beyond most Garou and Fera to render treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T09:42:03-07:00","id":620177,"title":"","content":"I think a major problem with the Children of Gaia are depicted is that people have a skewed vision of of Unicorn. It seems to be more the unicorn/My Little Pony that young girls love combined with hippies. This is why so many depictions fail. The Unicorn of legend is very different. Developers and writers should have emphasized the aspects of unicorn in actual legend as inspiration.<br /> <br /> The Unicorns of legend were representation of the power and majesty of the virgin wilderness. If the Unicorn was in an area, the forest remained untouched because ordinary people couldn't enter there without risking their lives. They were wild animals, and were very dangerous to humans because the wilderness could be very dangerous. Only the pure and innocent - children and especially virgin maidens - could approach and even tame them. Their horn did have mystical powers of healing, but that wasn't their main thing.<br /> <br /> I think a better way in depicting them is that they/Unicorn wants to restore the harmony and balance as the world was back in the days of young. This does not mean a return to Earth before Man like the Red Talons, but accepting man as part of nature, but integrating him into a more appropriate &quot;Gaian&quot; mindset. Harmony, not peace, should be the goal. Obviously peace can be a big part of that, but harmony in and of itself is not peace. This is why they strive to unite the Tribes and push humans into a better lifestyle. They believe in purity and innocence and are commanded by Unicorn to protect that, so that is why they especially seek to protect children and heal the exploited. But they are not weak pacifists.<br /> <br /> In my games, I always emphasize &quot;<i>Unicorn is not a tame animal</i>&quot;. If I have a unicorn spirit, I have it act like a wild mustang - very energetic, strong, and independent. I do have the burned out hippies and such, but there is always evidence that this aspect of the tribe is how the Wyrm is trying to destroy the Children of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T14:01:55-07:00","id":620474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=619808#post619808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Another one of the <i>really </i>goofy things in CoG: Revised was Hack, the lupus of the pack, actually <i>conversing </i>with his homid packmates not only while he's in lupus form, but doing it <i>in the full view of human bystanders</i>. Which means that humans are seeing three or four people talking to a wolf (yes, a <i>wolf</i>, Hack does <i>not </i>look like a dog) <i>and the wolf actually barking back as if in response</i>. &quot;Why no, honored elder, we haven't been breaching the Veil merely by having loud arguments with our lupus member in full view at public places with lots of humans about, why do you ask?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:36px\">*HEADDESK*</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I am put off by the book as much as a number of people here, but I will say that at least for *that* specific point they *do* provide an in-book explanation (if not shown directly in the panel/story, itself, as such) via the Gift &quot;Domestic Seeming&quot;. It's meta-narrative level that while *we*, the reader, see Hack as a wolf, he appears as a dog to others who are present. (Now, granted, that's just as ridiculous in a diner setting, too, but is at least less weird/disturbing as having a wolf there. I have, in a couple areas, been to local bars/diners where a pet or two &quot;made the rounds&quot; in the place and the locals were all cool with it -- &quot;Zoe&quot; a big mutt at Coolahan's, an Irish-redneck bar my friends and I used to frequent for years, comes to mind -- despite it being a breach of bar/restaurant ordinances, so I've seen it myself in Real Life(tm). However, that's pressing things a bit if the &quot;kids&quot; aren't local and the dog at the booth isn't a local's pet... still, that scene, given the meta-context provided, is by far the least sinful thing of the book, writing-wise, so I feel compelled to give it a pass....)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T14:54:16-07:00","id":622691,"title":"","content":"Overall, I'd go with the original tribebook. (Interesting fact that there was a CoG that threw himself into the Eater-Of-Souls along with the Croatan.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T16:10:42-07:00","id":622779,"title":"","content":"You know, with Lady Luck being a Totem, an excellent Totem for the Children of Gaia that would have made them far, far more interesting and compelling to play would have been the Totem, Uncle Leverage, a Totem who embodies knowing what you need to have over your opponent in order to get them to do the right thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T19:10:05-07:00","id":623018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=622779#post622779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, with Lady Luck being a Totem, an excellent Totem for the Children of Gaia that would have made them far, far more interesting and compelling to play would have been the Totem, Uncle Leverage, a Totem who embodies knowing what you need to have over your opponent in order to get them to do the right thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that.<br /> <br /> I like that a lot.<br /> <br /> #Ganked","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T14:01:23-07:00","id":624624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad?p=622779#post622779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, with Lady Luck being a Totem, an excellent Totem for the Children of Gaia that would have made them far, far more interesting and compelling to play would have been the Totem, Uncle Leverage, a Totem who embodies knowing what you need to have over your opponent in order to get them to do the right thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which &quot;Lady Luck&quot; totem are you referring to? There's no official totem named Lady Luck. Are you referring to Momentum from Book of the City, the totem also known as &quot;Winning Streak&quot; or &quot;Hot Hands?&quot; You know, the totem that is notorious for being a pack's temporary totem because her streak of luck that her children get <i>always </i>runs out at the worst possible moment?<br /> <br /> Who is this lady Luck totem you're referring to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thanked